From d3dffa8b64b521661641482372ee6146ea54a37e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:31:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(update-pause): a pause in a gateway-owned chat
 goes to the owner's FIFO; a late continuation says when it paused

laptop-1 2026-11-13 (t_01a1d4920ce3cbf4): a notice turn in Desktop backend pid 81192 paused for a core
update at 00:55 PST; the update did not apply. For 87 min every continuation was refused at the slot
claim ("canonical ledger holds queued work" -> "another live owner") while the gateway ran 9 turns of
the same chat, and the other backends held back because the marker's writer was alive. At 02:24 the
next backend replayed the 2 h old, already handled notice as "Your previous turn was interrupted".

Root cause: the marker's custodian (its writer pid) and the chat's turn custodian (the gateway's
durable ledger) were different and neither could finish the pause. The ownership refusal was treated
like a transient slot conflict (30 s backoff, nothing re-polls), although it never lifts while the
gateway keeps working. pause_note had one wording, written for the in-place continuation right after
the pause.

- A paused continuation refused by the gateway's ledger is queued in the owner's FIFO
  (owner_forward.forward_prompt, as prompt.submit does) and the pause is retired here. Work no running
  gateway will finish (unknown admission, no owner, refused or unconfirmed hand-off) retires it with a
  WARNING naming the reason and the request. A newer pause of the turn is never retired (compare on
  paused_at under the marker lock). Other slot refusals keep the existing backoff.
- "window ended without an update" logs once per pause across re-armed and carried-turn watchers.
- pause_note counts the stored transcript's user rows after paused_at. Once later turns ran (or it is
  queued behind the owner's turns, or the count is unreadable and the pause is >10 min old) the note
  names the pause time and age, says later turns ran since and to check before redoing anything,
  and never says the previous turn was interrupted. The new prefix is classified auto_continue
  (session_history legacy sniff, gateway replay stripper).

Tests: tests/tui_gateway/test_update_pause_ledger_owner.py (10 of 12 red on main, the 2 others pin
unchanged behaviour); 61 related files, 1490 tests green.
